:52.2,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.008530981896363254,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":60.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.002779506185712351,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":95.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.16307,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Silgan Holdings Inc., together with its subsidiaries, manufactures and sells rigid packaging solutions for consumer goods products in the United States and internationally. It operates through three segments: Dispensing and Specialty Closures, Metal Containers, and Custom Containers. The company offers integrated dispensing packaging solutions, proprietary metal and plastic specialty closures, and capping/sealing equipment and detection systems for fragrance and beauty, food, beverage, personal and health care, home care, and lawn and garden markets. It also provides steel and aluminum containers used by processors and packagers for food products, such as pet food, vegetables and fruits, soup, proteins, and other miscellaneous food products, as well as general line metal containers for products, including promotional products. In addition, the company offers custom designed polyethylene, polyethylene terephthalate, containers, thermoformed barrier and non-barrier bowls, trays for shelf-stable food products, and plastic caps, sifters and fitments for food and household products, including salad dressings, condiments, peanut butter, spices, liquid margarine, powdered drink mixes, and arts and crafts supplies. It markets its products primarily through direct sales force, as well as through a network of distributors, and an online shopping catalog. The company was founded in 1987 and is headquartered in Norwalk, Connecticut.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Adam J. Greenlee | President, CEO & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $2.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 17K people. Revenue per employee of $374K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 5%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $24K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Silgan Holdings Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $4.3B market cap on $6.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 16% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $423M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.53\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 16% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 48% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 21% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","21 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Consumer Cyclical peers","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Silgan Holdings (SLGN) Stock Climbed, What Is Behind The Latest Attention?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-slgn/silgan-holdings/news/silgan-holdings-slgn-stock-cl